# Areeb 30-chain taxonomy

Grouping 30-chain reads these four headers on **all three** catalogs. They are **not** the PE columns `Category` / `Department` / `Sub-Category` / `Sub-Department`.

| Header | Graph slot |
|---|---|
| `Category (Areeb)` | category |
| `Product Type (Areeb)` | product-type |
| `Product Style (Areeb)` | product-style |
| `Department (Areeb)` | department |

Code: `shared/areeb_taxonomy.py`. One-off fill: `python scripts/fill_areeb_taxonomy.py`. Future CL rows: `fill_from_seeds.py --steps areeb`.

## Custom Label — warehouse standard (`cl_standard`)

**Never copy BTC, Uneek, PE, Brand, or supplier cells into the four Areeb columns.** Study input was last-year ShipStation SKUs + the live CL `Gender Apparel` list (328 values, 0 blank). Fill values come from the warehouse system in `shared/areeb_taxonomy.py`. Refill **overwrites** all four Areeb cells on every CL row.

| Areeb column | How it is filled |
|---|---|
| `Category (Areeb)` | Product family from Gender Apparel (`T-SHIRTS`, `SWEATSHIRTS AND HOODIES`, `POLO SHIRTS`, `Stickers`, `Iron-On`, `Bags`, …). |
| `Product Type (Areeb)` | Type inside that family (`MENS SHORT SLEEVE T-SHIRT`, `Childrens T-Shirt`, `Sticker`, …). |
| `Product Style (Areeb)` | Style token from Gender Apparel (`Heavy Cotton`, `Softstyle`, `Valueweight`, `Classic`, `A4`, `BG125J`). **Not Brand.** |
| `Department (Areeb)` | **Gender only:** `Mens` / `Womens` / `Kids` / `Unisex` / `General`. Not raw Gender Apparel. Non-apparel (bags, stickers, mugs, iron-on, headwear, hospitality) → `General`. Hi-vis without kids/womens → `Unisex`. Adult garments with no gender word → `Mens`. |

Lookup order for one Gender Apparel string:

1. Exact table `CL_STANDARD_RULES` (legacy names + codes: `Mens-T-Shirt`, `5000`, `C800T-BS`, …)
2. Prefixes: `DTF-IronOn*` / `IronOn*` → Iron-On; `BG-*` / `PC-*` / `WB-*` / tote/backpack → Bags; `Cap-*` → HEADWEAR
3. Pattern engine on Gender Apparel words (hoodie, polo, trouser, hi-vis, …) + brand-prefix strip (`FOTL` / `FOLT` / `GILDAN` / `Uneek` / …) for style

Examples: `Mens-T-Shirt` → T-SHIRTS / MENS SHORT SLEEVE T-SHIRT / T-Shirt / Mens. `FOTL Mens Valueweight T` → … / Valueweight / Mens. `GILDAN Heavy Blend Adult Crewneck Sweatshirt` → SWEATSHIRTS AND HOODIES / Mens Sweatshirts & Hoodies / Heavy Blend / Mens. `Sticker` → Stickers / Sticker / Sticker / General. `Kids-T-Shirt-Hoodie` → Sets / T-Shirt and Hoodie / Kids Set / Kids.

## BTC Product Data (Plain / Packs only)

Join: UID (Plain `SKU`, Packs `Item 1 SKU`). Fallback: `Product Code` → BTC `SPC` (first UID on that SPC) — Plain and Packs. **Not used for Custom Label Areeb.**

| Areeb column | BTC column |
|---|---|
| `Category (Areeb)` | `Department` |
| `Product Type (Areeb)` | `Sub Department` |
| `Product Style (Areeb)` | `Brand` |
| `Department (Areeb)` | `Description` |

## Uneek Product Data (Plain / Packs only)

Join: `Short Code` (Plain `SKU`). Fallback: `Product Code`. **Not used for Custom Label Areeb.**

| Areeb column | Uneek column |
|---|---|
| `Category (Areeb)` | `Category` |
| `Product Type (Areeb)` | `Product Name` |
| `Product Style (Areeb)` | `Full Description` |
| `Department (Areeb)` | `Gender` |

Uneek `Department (Areeb)` is Gender; BTC `Department (Areeb)` is garment Description. Same column, two vocabularies — supervisor map 8 Sep 2026. Custom Label Department (Areeb) is warehouse gender only (`Mens` / `Womens` / `Kids` / `Unisex` / `General`).

## Plain / Packs

- Plain fill is **blank-only**. Lookup: `SKU` → BTC UID, else `SKU` → Uneek Short Code, else `Product Code` → BTC SPC, else leftover system `plain_leftover`.
- Packs (`01-Database`): `Item 1 SKU` → BTC UID, else `Product Code` → BTC SPC, else Uneek Short Code / Product Code. Never copy Packs `Description` (eBay HTML) into `Department (Areeb)`. Blank-only.

## Plain leftover (`plain_leftover`)

Used only when UID, Uneek Short Code, and BTC SPC all miss. Also fills **holes** on a supplier hit (example: Uneek `Category` blank → leftover Category only). Does **not** overwrite filled BTC/Uneek cells. Values stay in BTC language. **Not** Custom Label gender-only Department.

| Areeb column | How it is filled |
|---|---|
| `Category (Areeb)` | Family from Plain `Description` using BTC Department words (`T-SHIRTS`, `OUTERWEAR`, `SWEATSHIRTS AND HOODIES`, …). Last resort `Accessories`. |
| `Product Type (Areeb)` | Type from Description + gender words, using BTC Sub Department (`Ladies Short Sleeve T-Shirts`, `Childrens jackets`, …). |
| `Product Style (Areeb)` | Plain `Brand`. |
| `Department (Areeb)` | Plain `Description` (same slot as BTC Description). |

Gender words in Description pick the Sub Department only (`Girl's` / `Kid's` → Childrens, `Women's` / `Ladies` → Ladies, `Unisex` → Unisex, else Mens). They are **not** written into `Department (Areeb)`.

